# Soulcoil Viper: "Activate only as a sorcery" (CR 307.5, 602.5d): only during its controller's main phase with the stack empty. The Viper
# came in on turn 1, so it can use its {T} on turn 3. With a Black Lotus on the stack in the main phase, and in the end step, Bot1 cannot
# activate it targeting the Memnite Bot2 Bolted on turn 2 (the Swamp is untapped and could pay {B}); the Viper stays.

[Bot1 Deck]
Memnite
Black Lotus
Black Lotus
Soulcoil Viper
Swamp x3
Swamp x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Soulcoil Viper.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
! Bot1.Battlefield.Soulcoil Viper.Activate(Bot1.Graveyard.Memnite)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.End]
! Bot1.Battlefield.Soulcoil Viper.Activate(Bot1.Graveyard.Memnite)

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Soulcoil Viper.Tapped = false
Bot1.Graveyard = Memnite; Black Lotus
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Tapped = false
